#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# disjoint_q

#% text
# `disjoint_q(xs, ys)` is `true` when the lists `xs` and `ys` have no element in common.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Elements are compared by identity: `1` and `1.0` differ.

#% item
# `intersecting_q` is the opposite.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
disjoint_q([1, 2], [3, 4])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
disjoint_q([1, 2], [2, 3])
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
disjoint_q([], [1])
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `intersecting_q`, `intersection`, `is_subset`
